From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:37:49 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 21/50] Plutonium: seat management through logind

With --plutonium-logind-session=<id>, Ash is the controller of that logind
session (TakeControl), the way compositors started from a VT are. DRM and
input devices, libinput's included, are opened with TakeDevice. On
PauseDevice (another VT in front), display control is relinquished
without touching the hardware and the input devices are closed and given
back; on ResumeDevice for the card, display control is taken back with a
forced configuration and the input devices are opened again.

Ctrl+Alt+F1..F12 switch VTs (Seat.SwitchTo): the kernel keyboard is off.
Ctrl+Alt+Backspace ends the session with SIGTERM. logind restores the VT
whenever Ash exits, crashes included.

In the GPU process, SetMaster/DropMaster count the file's master state,
which logind changes, rather than their own ioctl's result.
